          "path": "_m/tpc/le/ic/es/te/leicester/jewry-wall-and-st-nicholas.jpg",
          "filename": "Jewry Wall and St Nicholas.jpg",
          "caption": "The Jewry Wall and St Nicholas' Church in Leicester, England. The wall is the second largest piece of surviving civil Roman building in Britain, and is both a Scheduled Monument and a Grade I listed building. Originally it separated the Palaestra from the Frigidarium at Ratae Corieltauvorum's baths. St Nicholas' Church is also Grade I listed, and dates from AD 880.",
